NAME
    globx - expand a filename glob into a list of files
            (#include "../lib_globx.c")

SYNOPSIS
    #include "../lib_globx.c"     (includes lib_fs.c and lib_glob.c)
    char out[24 * GSLOT];         GSLOT = 64
    n = glob_expand(pattern, out, 24);

DESCRIPTION
    glob_expand(pat, out, maxn) -> the number of matches
      pat    the pattern word (ends at NUL or a space), * and ? in its
             last component only: "*.TXT" (the current directory) or
             "/MAN/C*"
      out    maxn slots of GSLOT (64) bytes; slot i = the directory
             part of pat + the i-th matching name, NUL-ended, so it
             opens the way the bare word would (a relative prefix stays
             relative to the current directory)
      maxn   the slot count; matches past it are dropped
    isglob(w) is 1 when the word w (ends at NUL or a space) holds * or
    ?.

    Only FILES match (not directories, not . and ..), in the order the
    directory stores them. The directory is read on a handle of
    glob_expand's own, closed again before it returns.

LIMITS
    The directory part must leave room in a slot for a 12-character
    name (about 50 characters), or nothing matches. The name pattern
    is cut at 15 characters.

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: opendir, readdir and fclose on its
    own handle instead of FOPENDIR/SYS_OPENCWD, FNEXT and SYS_DIRENTRY,
    so the FSDIRBUF page juggling is gone (every Y1/OS handle owns its
    buffer); the names come from ent_name().
    Ported from P8X os/commands/lib_globx.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    glob, stdin, cat, cp, mv, del
